bilbo keeps durable memory for coding agents: it remembers their sessions and
the pages they cite, and recalls them when a later session asks.

[1mUsage:[22m [36mbilbo [39m[2m<verb>[22m[36m [[39m[2m<args>[22m[36m][39m

[1mVerbs:[22m
  [1mremember[22m  Keep files as entries; a later run keeps what grew or changed
  [1mrecall[22m    Search everything bilbo keeps and print the chunks that match best
  [1mread[22m      Print an entry: its outline, or its records a page at a time
  [1mreindex[22m   Rebuild the catalog and the search index from the store
  [1mconfig[22m    Show each setting, its value and where it came from

[2mRun '[22m[36mbilbo [39m[2m<verb>[22m[36m --help[39m[2m' for its options, output and exit codes.[22m
[1mDocs:[22m [2mhttps://github.com/delucca/bilbo/wiki[22m
